WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.340 --> 00:00:04.279
Captain Francis Pike leads his team across
the arctic tundra.

00:00:04.279 --> 00:00:08.450
In the distance, they can see the city of
Audapaupadopolis.

00:00:08.450 --> 00:00:13.510
It floats 7.8 kilometers above the ground
and is filled with mysteries and treasures

00:00:13.510 --> 00:00:16.880
beyond even the Foundation’s wildest dreams.

00:00:16.880 --> 00:00:22.671
It is September of 1933 when the SCP Foundation
first catches wind of something odd going

00:00:22.671 --> 00:00:24.080
on in the arctic.

00:00:24.080 --> 00:00:29.210
A British airman named Sir George Dansen flies
over the North Sea heading to Norway.

00:00:29.210 --> 00:00:33.680
After he lands in Oslo, Dansen begins ranting
about a floating city.

00:00:33.680 --> 00:00:38.910
The Foundation immediately disseminates contradictory
information and manipulates the story to include

00:00:38.910 --> 00:00:43.750
that Dansen had been drinking during his flight,
so everything he is saying is probably the

00:00:43.750 --> 00:00:45.820
result of a drunken hallucination.

00:00:45.820 --> 00:00:51.840
While SCP agents spread lies, the Foundation
immediately launches an investigation.

00:00:51.840 --> 00:00:56.149
The team that is sent to the arctic confirms
what Dansen claims to have seen.

00:00:56.149 --> 00:00:59.000
There is indeed a floating city there.

00:00:59.000 --> 00:01:03.510
Now Captain Pike and his team stare at the
island in the sky as their hot-air balloons

00:01:03.510 --> 00:01:05.249
are filled behind them.

00:01:05.249 --> 00:01:09.729
The arctic wind whips up small snow tornadoes
as the temperature plummets.

00:01:09.729 --> 00:01:13.420
The balloons are ready, and Pike orders his
men to board.

00:01:13.420 --> 00:01:17.619
They lift off from the ground and pull their
parka hoods over their heads to protect them

00:01:17.619 --> 00:01:20.750
from the arctic blasts at high altitudes.

00:01:20.750 --> 00:01:24.479
Pike and his team slowly drift over the city
of Audapaupadopolis.

00:01:24.479 --> 00:01:27.849
When they are somewhat in the middle of the
floating island, the hot-air balloons are

00:01:27.849 --> 00:01:30.790
lowered and the team lands without incident.

00:01:30.790 --> 00:01:35.929
To their surprise, the exploratory team finds
that the floating city has its own micro-climate,

00:01:35.929 --> 00:01:38.680
which is much more pleasant than the frigid
arctic.

00:01:38.680 --> 00:01:40.299
They remove their winter gear.

00:01:40.299 --> 00:01:42.840
“Proceed with caution,” Pike tells his
men.

00:01:42.840 --> 00:01:45.889
“We have no idea what we’re going to find
in the city.”

00:01:45.889 --> 00:01:51.130
The architecture is clearly old, but not exactly
like anything on Earth today.

00:01:51.130 --> 00:01:56.389
It seems to be a conglomerate of ancient Mesopotamian
design mixed with the design features of several

00:01:56.389 --> 00:01:57.959
other cultures.

00:01:57.959 --> 00:02:02.130
Many of the buildings that line the stone
streets are crumbling and the city overall

00:02:02.130 --> 00:02:03.799
is in ruins.

00:02:03.799 --> 00:02:06.689
Pike leads his team down a series of roads.

00:02:06.689 --> 00:02:10.190
Scientists photograph and take notes on the
city for Foundation records.

00:02:10.190 --> 00:02:15.250
SCP agents check around every corner to make
sure there is nothing hiding in the shadows.

00:02:15.250 --> 00:02:17.909
The team comes to a crossroads.

00:02:17.909 --> 00:02:18.909
“Halt!”

00:02:18.909 --> 00:02:19.909
Pike shouts.

00:02:19.909 --> 00:02:23.810
Standing in front of them is an old man with
long grey hair and a white beard.

00:02:23.810 --> 00:02:26.549
He seems to be of Middle Eastern descent.

00:02:26.549 --> 00:02:27.930
“Hello friends!”

00:02:27.930 --> 00:02:29.159
the old man says.

00:02:29.159 --> 00:02:30.569
“Welcome to Audapaupadopolis.

00:02:30.569 --> 00:02:33.310
I am the caretaker of the city.

00:02:33.310 --> 00:02:34.810
I have been expecting you.

00:02:34.810 --> 00:02:36.280
Please follow me.”

00:02:36.280 --> 00:02:39.730
The old man turns around and proceeds down
the causeway.

00:02:39.730 --> 00:02:41.319
Pike hesitates for a moment.

00:02:41.319 --> 00:02:44.319
“Stay alert,” he whispers to the agents
behind him.

00:02:44.319 --> 00:02:47.359
Then he begins to follow the old man down
the street.

00:02:47.359 --> 00:02:51.300
As Pike walks he takes in the grandeur that
the city once held.

00:02:51.300 --> 00:02:55.750
The roads are as wide as the main avenues
back in London, while the buildings, although

00:02:55.750 --> 00:02:59.410
in shambles, still retain some of their ancient
beauty.

00:02:59.410 --> 00:03:02.310
Pike begins to walk a little faster to catch
up with the old man.

00:03:02.310 --> 00:03:04.640
“What happened here?” he asks.

00:03:04.640 --> 00:03:05.849
The man turns his head.

00:03:05.849 --> 00:03:09.450
“All will be revealed soon Francis Pike;
just be patient.”

00:03:09.450 --> 00:03:12.090
“How do you know my name?” asks Pike.

00:03:12.090 --> 00:03:13.580
The old man smiles.

00:03:13.580 --> 00:03:17.280
They turn another corner and in front of them
is the Grand Hall.

00:03:17.280 --> 00:03:21.390
It seems to have survived whatever catastrophe
befell the rest of the city.

00:03:21.390 --> 00:03:25.360
Pike stops and stares up at the massive structure
with his mouth ajar.

00:03:25.360 --> 00:03:30.500
“Come,” says the old man as he motions
the SCP team to follow him up the steps into

00:03:30.500 --> 00:03:31.500
the main hall.

00:03:31.500 --> 00:03:32.500
“Let’s eat.”

00:03:32.500 --> 00:03:37.400
The old man prepares a simple meal, but one
that fills the stomachs and satisfies Pike

00:03:37.400 --> 00:03:38.400
and his men.

00:03:38.400 --> 00:03:42.599
At the conclusion of the meal, Captain Pike
approaches the mysterious man.

00:03:42.599 --> 00:03:46.989
“I feel like you deserve an explanation
as to who we are and why we’re here,”

00:03:46.989 --> 00:03:47.989
Pike says.

00:03:47.989 --> 00:03:49.329
The old man raises his hand.

00:03:49.329 --> 00:03:52.040
“You are from the Foundation,” he replies.

00:03:52.040 --> 00:03:55.660
“I already know all about the Foundation
and you Francis Pike.

00:03:55.660 --> 00:03:58.749
I have been waiting for you to arrive for
a long time.

00:03:58.749 --> 00:04:01.599
There are things I need to show you in the
city.

00:04:01.599 --> 00:04:05.739
There are old secrets and ancient relics from
the past that you were sent here to learn

00:04:05.739 --> 00:04:06.739
about.”

00:04:06.739 --> 00:04:08.060
Pike looks at the man and squints.

00:04:08.060 --> 00:04:09.519
“What are you talking about?

00:04:09.519 --> 00:04:11.159
How could you know we were coming?

00:04:11.159 --> 00:04:13.590
And what relics are you referring to exactly?”

00:04:13.590 --> 00:04:17.319
The old man grins and places a hand on Captain
Pike’s shoulder.

00:04:17.319 --> 00:04:20.180
Pike feels a longing emotion well up inside
of him.

00:04:20.180 --> 00:04:23.770
It’s as if he has been waiting for this
moment his whole life.

00:04:23.770 --> 00:04:25.240
“Come,” says the old man.

00:04:25.240 --> 00:04:27.419
“You and your men need rest.”

00:04:27.419 --> 00:04:31.520
He shows Pike and the exploration team to
several rooms down the hallway where they

00:04:31.520 --> 00:04:33.050
can set up for the night.

00:04:33.050 --> 00:04:35.259
The rooms are large and comfortable.

00:04:35.259 --> 00:04:39.340
“Sleep well Francis Pike, tomorrow I have
much to show you.”

00:04:39.340 --> 00:04:44.430
The old man leaves the room and proceeds down
the hallway to his small, humble, chamber.

00:04:44.430 --> 00:04:49.210
The next morning Pike and the other SCP agents
are greeted by the rising sun and the old

00:04:49.210 --> 00:04:51.680
man waiting for them on the steps of the Grand
Hall.

00:04:51.680 --> 00:04:53.550
He leads them through the city.

00:04:53.550 --> 00:04:57.950
“There are three temples I wish to show
you,” the old man says to Pike.

00:04:57.950 --> 00:05:02.090
“You will notice that their architecture
and imagery differ from most of the other

00:05:02.090 --> 00:05:03.740
structures in the city.

00:05:03.740 --> 00:05:07.800
Make sure you listen very carefully Francis
Pike, as what you're about to learn could

00:05:07.800 --> 00:05:09.270
save the universe…

00:05:09.270 --> 00:05:10.860
or perhaps destroy it.”

00:05:10.860 --> 00:05:12.379
Pike is speechless.

00:05:12.379 --> 00:05:14.360
All he can do is nod his head.

00:05:14.360 --> 00:05:20.010
The old man leads the SCP agents to the middle
of the city where the three temples reside.

00:05:20.010 --> 00:05:23.669
Each one has its own unique iconography and
style.

00:05:23.669 --> 00:05:28.229
The art seems to reflect important events
in history or subjects that hold significance

00:05:28.229 --> 00:05:29.520
in the past.

00:05:29.520 --> 00:05:32.530
The old man proceeds to walk towards the first
temple.

00:05:32.530 --> 00:05:37.099
Upon entering the structure there is a mural
of two naked people watching the horizon from

00:05:37.099 --> 00:05:38.550
a treeline.

00:05:38.550 --> 00:05:42.889
Behind them are a wolf and bear that seem
to be protectively standing guard.

00:05:42.889 --> 00:05:48.290
Directly opposite of this picture is a painting
of a figure holding a flaming sword on a hill.

00:05:48.290 --> 00:05:52.979
As Pike and his team enter the main hall they
are welcomed by a gigantic mural depicting

00:05:52.979 --> 00:05:55.000
the sun rising over Audapaupadopolis.

00:05:55.000 --> 00:06:00.330
“This is where the Temple of Sunrise gets
its name,” the old man says gesturing to

00:06:00.330 --> 00:06:02.330
the mural on the far wall.

00:06:02.330 --> 00:06:06.790
Below the sunrise is a golden man holding
a spear with a silver point.

00:06:06.790 --> 00:06:08.860
He wears a shining crown.

00:06:08.860 --> 00:06:12.860
Pike can’t help but notice that the man
in the mural looks similar to their guide,

00:06:12.860 --> 00:06:15.129
just a lot younger.

00:06:15.129 --> 00:06:19.220
Perhaps it is his son or a relative, Pike
thinks to himself.

00:06:19.220 --> 00:06:22.240
Above the sunrise is a dragon with green eyes.

00:06:22.240 --> 00:06:27.319
Engraved across the dragon’s body are the
words “THEY WILL KNOW WHAT IS”.

00:06:27.319 --> 00:06:30.569
The other walls contain images of the same
golden man.

00:06:30.569 --> 00:06:35.259
In one picture he stands at the foot of a
throne with a naked woman wrapped in snakes

00:06:35.259 --> 00:06:36.259
beside him.

00:06:36.259 --> 00:06:41.659
On another, the golden man sits on the throne
with an iron crown hovering above his head.

00:06:41.659 --> 00:06:44.449
Behind him are monoliths of five figures.

00:06:44.449 --> 00:06:49.419
One is made of gears and steel, another is
made of flesh and blood, the third is made

00:06:49.419 --> 00:06:55.669
of ice and stone, the fourth is made of stars,
and the final is made of eyes.

00:06:55.669 --> 00:06:59.220
The SCP agents in the room begin to buzz with
excitement.

00:06:59.220 --> 00:07:01.250
They start recording everything they see.

00:07:01.250 --> 00:07:03.939
“We must continue on,” the old man says.

00:07:03.939 --> 00:07:05.849
“There isn’t much time left.”

00:07:05.849 --> 00:07:10.370
Pike nods and orders a small team to stay
behind to continue documenting the Temple

00:07:10.370 --> 00:07:11.659
of Sunrise.

00:07:11.659 --> 00:07:15.110
The next building they enter is the Temple
of Sunset.

00:07:15.110 --> 00:07:18.439
Within its walls are maps of different towns
and landscapes.

00:07:18.439 --> 00:07:21.000
One of the maps is of Audapaupadopolis itself.

00:07:21.000 --> 00:07:26.000
The words “THE LANDS OF MEN” are scrolled
over the map in the entry hall.

00:07:26.000 --> 00:07:28.630
The old man stops at the opening to the main
gallery.

00:07:28.630 --> 00:07:30.889
“Prepare yourself Francis Pike.

00:07:30.889 --> 00:07:33.500
What you are about to witness will not be
pleasant.”

00:07:33.500 --> 00:07:37.310
They head into the next room where the temperature
immediately shoots up.

00:07:37.310 --> 00:07:39.970
“What the hell is producing all of that
heat?”

00:07:39.970 --> 00:07:40.970
Pike asks.

00:07:40.970 --> 00:07:45.310
There is nothing but crumbling walls and fallen
columns visible in the room.

00:07:45.310 --> 00:07:47.840
One of the scientists hollers from the back
of the group.

00:07:47.840 --> 00:07:48.840
“Jesus!

00:07:48.840 --> 00:07:50.719
Sir, I think you need to take a look at this.”

00:07:50.719 --> 00:07:54.409
He walks up to Pike and hands him a pair of
thermal imaging goggles.

00:07:54.409 --> 00:07:55.610
Pike puts them on.

00:07:55.610 --> 00:07:57.330
“Damn,” Pike mutters.

00:07:57.330 --> 00:08:01.650
With the thermal lenses on he can now see
a massive humanoid entity lying dead on the

00:08:01.650 --> 00:08:02.650
floor.

00:08:02.650 --> 00:08:06.800
His body is so large that it covers the murals
on three of the walls.

00:08:06.800 --> 00:08:10.740
Pike notices that the temperature in the room
is still continuing to increase as if the

00:08:10.740 --> 00:08:12.940
dead giant is radiating heat.

00:08:12.940 --> 00:08:20.490
The Foundation classifies the entity as SCP-4840-B.
It has six arms and six legs each connected

00:08:20.490 --> 00:08:23.180
by metal chains to iron flails at the end.

00:08:23.180 --> 00:08:26.740
A sigil has been brandished into the middle
of the entity’s chest.

00:08:26.740 --> 00:08:28.310
“What is that?”

00:08:28.310 --> 00:08:29.310
Pike asks.

00:08:29.310 --> 00:08:31.039
The old man just shakes his head.

00:08:31.039 --> 00:08:33.930
“One of the many who have fallen,” he
responds.

00:08:33.930 --> 00:08:40.030
The old man points to the only wall that is
not blocked by the massive body of SCP-4840-B

00:08:40.030 --> 00:08:41.330
and frowns.

00:08:41.330 --> 00:08:44.150
The golden man is depicted here as well.

00:08:44.150 --> 00:08:48.480
Pike can’t help but feel there is some sort
of connection between Audapaupadopolis, the

00:08:48.480 --> 00:08:52.210
old man, and the golden figure he keeps seeing
in the murals.

00:08:52.210 --> 00:08:57.440
In the Temple of Sunset the golden man sits
atop a white horse with his iron crown resting

00:08:57.440 --> 00:08:58.860
on his head.

00:08:58.860 --> 00:09:03.590
Behind him is a massive army of men and women
holding axes and swords.

00:09:03.590 --> 00:09:07.880
Across from the golden man and his army are
legions of green and grey figures with six

00:09:07.880 --> 00:09:10.910
eyes dressed in brilliantly colored clothing.

00:09:10.910 --> 00:09:14.460
An intense lightning storm appears to be amassing
in the distance.

00:09:14.460 --> 00:09:18.730
Captain Pike looks up at the ceiling to see
it covered in stars, however, he does not

00:09:18.730 --> 00:09:20.680
recognize any of the constellations.

00:09:20.680 --> 00:09:25.170
“Is the golden man I keep seeing y—”
but before Pike can finish his question, the

00:09:25.170 --> 00:09:26.310
old man cuts him off.

00:09:26.310 --> 00:09:27.600
“We must keep going.”

00:09:27.600 --> 00:09:29.530
He turns and exits the temple.

00:09:29.530 --> 00:09:33.700
Pike does not want to push the old man; he
seems to be a wealth of knowledge and the

00:09:33.700 --> 00:09:38.120
only way to learn more about Audapaupadopolis
and what it all means.

00:09:38.120 --> 00:09:42.960
They exit the Temple of Sunset and continue
to the final structure in the middle of the

00:09:42.960 --> 00:09:43.960
city.

00:09:43.960 --> 00:09:48.580
The old man leads Pike and the rest of the
SCP agents to the smallest temple of the three.

00:09:48.580 --> 00:09:50.930
He stops just outside of the doorway.

00:09:50.930 --> 00:09:53.730
“This is the Temple of Night,” he proclaims.

00:09:53.730 --> 00:09:56.840
“What you see on the surface is deceiving.

00:09:56.840 --> 00:09:59.000
This temple goes deep underground.

00:09:59.000 --> 00:10:04.070
It contains a labyrinth of passages that one
could get lost in forever, so please be careful.”

00:10:04.070 --> 00:10:05.450
“Aren’t you coming?”

00:10:05.450 --> 00:10:06.450
Pike asks.

00:10:06.450 --> 00:10:08.050
“No,” responds the old man.

00:10:08.050 --> 00:10:10.480
“I do not enter the Temple of Night…

00:10:10.480 --> 00:10:13.540
I have my reasons, which do not concern you.”

00:10:13.540 --> 00:10:17.330
Pike nods and then signals his men to follow
him into the temple.

00:10:17.330 --> 00:10:21.280
He notices that many of the murals in the
passageways and rooms of the Temple of Night

00:10:21.280 --> 00:10:25.950
depict the same image of a massive tree in
the middle of a vast forest.

00:10:25.950 --> 00:10:30.940
In each instance of the tree, there seem to
be red lights surrounding the base, human-like

00:10:30.940 --> 00:10:36.580
figures hanging from its branches, and structures
wrapped in vines surrounding the trunk.

00:10:36.580 --> 00:10:40.100
The hallways are illuminated by some unknown
light source.

00:10:40.100 --> 00:10:44.890
It is as if torches line the walls and give
off a dull yellowish glow, but there is no

00:10:44.890 --> 00:10:46.570
fire to be seen.

00:10:46.570 --> 00:10:51.980
Embedded in the walls are sarcophagi with
intricate carvings in their stone casings.

00:10:51.980 --> 00:10:57.510
Pike can’t help but notice scratching sounds
coming from within the sarcophagi as if someone,

00:10:57.510 --> 00:11:01.510
or something, is trying to claw its way out.

00:11:01.510 --> 00:11:05.130
The exploration team reaches the innermost
chamber of the temple.

00:11:05.130 --> 00:11:08.820
There is a staircase in the middle of the
room that descends below the floor.

00:11:08.820 --> 00:11:12.540
However, its entrance is covered by rubble
from a collapsed wall.

00:11:12.540 --> 00:11:15.160
Suddenly an SCP agent runs up to Captain Pike.

00:11:15.160 --> 00:11:17.330
“Sir, I think you should see this.”

00:11:17.330 --> 00:11:20.760
Pike follows the man back through a series
of twists and turns.

00:11:20.760 --> 00:11:22.680
He stops at a closed door.

00:11:22.680 --> 00:11:26.080
The Foundation seal is carved into the wood.

00:11:26.080 --> 00:11:30.670
It seems as if the carving has been there
for a long time, which is impossible since

00:11:30.670 --> 00:11:35.010
they are the first SCP team to explore the
city of Audapaupadopolis.

00:11:35.010 --> 00:11:37.960
The agent pushes open the door and Pike steps
in.

00:11:37.960 --> 00:11:40.610
He is astonished by what he finds.

00:11:40.610 --> 00:11:44.120
It seems he has been transported to an abandoned
Foundation site.

00:11:44.120 --> 00:11:48.710
All of the lights are off, but he can tell
that it is some kind of central command center

00:11:48.710 --> 00:11:51.780
due to the screens and setup of the space.

00:11:51.780 --> 00:11:58.120
Painted in black block letters on one of the
walls is: Site-00-00-00.

00:11:58.120 --> 00:12:01.760
Pike quickly exits back through the entranceway
and shuts the door behind him.

00:12:01.760 --> 00:12:04.690
He looks at the SCP agent who brought him
to the room.

00:12:04.690 --> 00:12:08.140
“Secure this door and make sure no one goes
in… or comes out.

00:12:08.140 --> 00:12:10.240
Do I make myself clear?”

00:12:10.240 --> 00:12:12.320
Pike orders his men to exit the temple.

00:12:12.320 --> 00:12:16.390
After everyone is out, Captain Pike walks
over to the old man who is sitting on the

00:12:16.390 --> 00:12:17.390
steps outside.

00:12:17.390 --> 00:12:20.570
“Did you find what you were looking for
Francis Pike?”

00:12:20.570 --> 00:12:21.730
the old man asks.

00:12:21.730 --> 00:12:23.510
Captain Pike shakes his head.

00:12:23.510 --> 00:12:27.230
He stares down, eyes wide, at the stone steps
of the temple.

00:12:27.230 --> 00:12:28.980
“I see,” says the old man.

00:12:28.980 --> 00:12:31.750
“I have something else to show you Francis
Pike.”

00:12:31.750 --> 00:12:36.170
The old man leads Pike back to the Grand Hall
that they had slept in the night before.

00:12:36.170 --> 00:12:40.050
He brings him through a series of passageways
and down a staircase.

00:12:40.050 --> 00:12:41.840
They stop in front of a large door.

00:12:41.840 --> 00:12:44.390
“Open it,” the old man whispers.

00:12:44.390 --> 00:12:48.060
Captain Francis Pike walks up to the door
and pushes it open.

00:12:48.060 --> 00:12:52.680
On the other side is endless darkness from
which he hears his own voice speaking to him

00:12:52.680 --> 00:12:54.010
through the ether.

00:12:54.010 --> 00:12:56.660
Pike begins to walk towards the darkness.

00:12:56.660 --> 00:13:00.470
The old man places his hand on Pike’s shoulder
and pulls him back.

00:13:00.470 --> 00:13:01.690
Then he shuts the door.

00:13:01.690 --> 00:13:07.330
“The light of the world has long since left
that place, and mortal men can no longer walk

00:13:07.330 --> 00:13:08.700
it,” says the old man.

00:13:08.700 --> 00:13:11.740
“I needed to show it to you as a warning.

00:13:11.740 --> 00:13:14.320
Things are not always what they seem Francis
Pike.”

00:13:14.320 --> 00:13:19.360
That night Pike lies awake staring at the
ceiling of the Grand Hall thinking about the

00:13:19.360 --> 00:13:20.360
old man.

00:13:20.360 --> 00:13:23.520
He sits up and begins jotting down his thoughts.

00:13:23.520 --> 00:13:29.860
In his official report, he identifies the
old man as SCP-4840-A, but in his journal,

00:13:29.860 --> 00:13:32.690
he can’t help but refer to him as a friend.

00:13:32.690 --> 00:13:36.190
There is something about the old man, something
special.

00:13:36.190 --> 00:13:42.690
Pike knows there is much more to his story,
and the story of the Flying City of Audapaupadopolis.

